    <ReasonableCauseExplanation documentId="R000003" softwareId="24021167" softwareVersionNum="v1.00">
      <ExplanationTxt>By way of background, the Taxpayer submitted Form 1024 on December 5, 2024, requesting a determination of its tax-exempt status. We did not receive a determination letter from the IRS confirming that status until June 16, 2025. Despite multiple attempts, taxpayer was unable to electronically file Form 990-EZ because the IRS system did not yet recognize our TIN as being associated with an active tax-exempt entity. To avoid any missed or delayed filings, we submitted a hard-copy return as a precaution on May 8, 2025; however, that return was subsequently returned by the IRS on June 12, 2025 stating the filing needed to be made electronically. We respectively request that any penalties potentially assessable under IRC Sec/on 6652 for a late or incomplete return be waived. The Taxpayer made every effort to comply with the filing requirements, and the inability to do so electronically was due to reasonable cause.</ExplanationTxt>
